# Knowledge Sync Classification Specification

## Purpose

This specification defines how code and data changes are classified in 
terms of their **knowledge impact**.

The goal is to ensure that:

* architectural and behavioral changes are reflected in the Knowledge 
Vault;
* non-structural changes do not produce noise;
* sync-check tooling operates on **Vault-derived rules**, not path 
heuristics.

---

## Core Principle

A change is considered **knowledge-bearing** if it affects:

* system architecture;
* domain model;
* invariants or rules;
* cross-module protocols;
* data contracts;
* documented behavior.

A change is **not knowledge-bearing** if it affects only:

* presentation;
* styling;
* test verification;
* runtime artifacts;
* content within existing schemas.

---

## Classification Model

All changes MUST be classified into one of four categories:

### 1. ALWAYS (Hard Fail)

Changes that **always require Knowledge Vault validation or update**.

These changes affect **architectural contracts** or **invariants**.

---

### 2. SOMETIMES (Soft Warning)

Changes that **may require Knowledge Vault updates**, depending on 
context.

These changes affect **control flow**, **integration points**, or **data 
wiring**.

---

### 3. NEVER (Silent Pass)

Changes that **never require Knowledge Vault updates**.

These changes are strictly **presentation** or **verification-only**.

---

### 4. SKIP (Mechanical Ignore)

Changes that are **not relevant to classification**.

These include system artifacts and non-project files.

---

## Classification Rules

### Rule Group A — System Layers

(Source: `architecture--system--overall-structure.md`)

| Layer          | Path                                                   
| Classification    | Notes                                 |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ 
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Vault (media)  | `vault/arts/**`, `vault/hopper/**`, `vault/streams/**` 
| NEVER             | Binary assets                         |
| Vault (data)   | `vault/json/**`                                        
| SOMETIMES         | Schema vs content not distinguishable |
| Knowledge      | `knowledge/**`                                         
| SKIP              | Validated by separate system          |
| Rules          | `rules/**`                                             
| ALWAYS            | Source of invariants                  |
| Docs           | `Docs/**`                                              
| SOMETIMES / NEVER | See Rule Group E                      |
| Infrastructure | `docker/**`                                            
| SOMETIMES         | Topology may change architecture      |

---

### Rule Group B — Frontend Layering (FSD)

(Source: `architecture--system--frontend-layering.md`, 
`invariant--architecture--downward-only-dependencies.md`)

| Path                                             | Classification | 
Rationale                                    |
| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------- | 
-------------------------------------------- |
| `entities/{art,block,stream,event,homeDoc}/**`   | ALWAYS         | 
Domain model is fixed and controlled         |
| `entities/* (non-domain)`                        | SOMETIMES      | Type 
contracts and supporting modules        |
| `shared/nav/**`                                  | ALWAYS         | 
Journey protocol invariant                   |
| `shared/state/**`                                | ALWAYS         | 
Store hierarchy = architecture               |
| `features/*/session/**`, `features/*/context/**` | SOMETIMES      | 
Control plane logic                          |
| `features/*/api/**`                              | SOMETIMES      | API 
contracts                                |
| `features/*/ui/**`                               | NEVER          | UI 
must not contain business logic           |
| `shared/ui/**`                                   | NEVER          | UI 
primitives                                |
| `shared/galleryLayouts/**`                       | NEVER          | 
Presentation only                            |
| `shared/lib/**`                                  | SOMETIMES [C]  | 
Mixed domain + utility logic                 |
| `app/router.tsx`                                 | ALWAYS         | 
Route map is part of architecture            |
| `app/** (excluding router)`                      | SOMETIMES      | 
Provider chains                              |
| `pages/admin/**`                                 | SOMETIMES [C]  | Some 
pages contain logic (legacy violations) |
| `pages/public/**`                                | SOMETIMES [C]  | Data 
wiring and rendering pipelines          |
| `*.css`                                          | NEVER          | 
Styling only                                 |
| `*.test.ts`, `__tests__/**`                      | NEVER          | 
Tests do not define architecture             |

---

### Rule Group C — Backend

(Source: `decision--data--json-vault-no-database.md`, domain model)

| Path                           | Classification | Rationale            |
| ------------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------- |
| `admin-backend/app/models/**`  | ALWAYS         | API contracts        |
| `admin-backend/app/repos/**`   | ALWAYS         | Storage patterns     |
| `admin-backend/app/routers/**` | ALWAYS         | Endpoint definitions |
| `admin-backend/app/main.py`    | SOMETIMES      | Router mounting      |

---

### Rule Group D — Domain and Protocol Invariants

| Area            | Path                                           | 
Classification | Source                               |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | 
-------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Domain entities | `entities/{art,block,stream,event,homeDoc}/**` | 
ALWAYS         | `entities-are-finite-and-controlled` |
| Journey system  | `shared/nav/**`                                | 
ALWAYS         | `all-cross-editor-flows-use-journey` |
| State system    | `shared/state/**`                              | 
ALWAYS         | `no-global-data-in-react-contexts`   |
| Data contracts  | backend models/repos                           | 
ALWAYS         | data decision docs                   |

---

### Rule Group E — Documentation

| Pattern                                                                | 
Classification | Notes                      |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | 
-------------- | -------------------------- |
| `Docs/plans/**`, `Docs/*IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN*`                          | 
NEVER          | Task-scoped                |
| `Docs/DEVELOPMENT_BLOG/**`, `Docs/projectBlog/**`                      | 
NEVER          | Informational              |
| `Docs/KANBAN/**`, `Docs/bugs/**`                                       | 
NEVER          | Operational                |
| `Docs/mds/**`, migration/setup notes                                   | 
NEVER          | Non-architectural          |
| `Docs/MANUAL_TEST_PLAN*`, audits                                       | 
NEVER          | Snapshot artifacts         |
| `Docs/COMM.log`                                                        | 
SKIP           | Conversation log           |
| `Docs/*SPEC*`, `*CONTRACT*`, `*ARCHITECTURE*`, agreements, `PROJECT_*` | 
SOMETIMES      | May define system behavior |
| Other Docs                                                             | 
SOMETIMES [C]  | Conservative default       |

---

## Conservative Classification [C]

Some paths cannot be reliably classified at the directory level.

These are intentionally marked as SOMETIMES:

* `shared/lib/**`
* `pages/public/**`
* `pages/admin/**`
* `vault/json/**`
* `docker/**`
* unspecified `Docs/**`

Reason:

* mixed responsibilities within the same directory;
* lack of machine-detectable structural boundaries;
* limitations of path-based classification.

These cases MUST produce **warnings, not failures**.

---

## Mechanical Rules (SKIP)

The following checks do not require Knowledge Vault:

* empty or invalid input paths;
* path normalization;
* binary files and generated artifacts;
* git parsing;
* `knowledge/**` validation (handled separately).

---

## Sync-Check Behavior

### ALWAYS

* block execution;
* require Knowledge Vault validation/update;
* include reference to relevant Vault documents.

### SOMETIMES

* allow execution;
* emit warning;
* include guidance on what to verify.

### NEVER

* allow execution silently.

### SKIP

* ignore.

---

## Explainability Requirement

Every classification MUST be explainable:

* which rule group was applied;
* which Vault document defines the rule;
* why the path falls into this category.

Example:

```
ALWAYS: shared/nav/transporter.ts

Reason:
- invariant: all cross-editor flows use Journey
- document: invariant--navigation--all-cross-editor-flows-use-journey.md
```

---

## Limitations

* Path-based classification cannot distinguish:

  * schema vs content changes in JSON;
  * domain logic vs utility logic in mixed directories;
* Some architectural violations (e.g., logic in UI or pages) reduce 
accuracy;
* The system is intentionally conservative in ambiguous cases.

---

## Future Improvements

* Move domain logic out of `shared/lib/**`;
* enforce strict FSD boundaries;
* introduce JSON schema-aware diffing;
* classify Docs using metadata instead of path patterns;
* integrate AST-based analysis for higher precision.

---

## Summary

This system replaces flat heuristics with a **Vault-driven classification 
model**.

* Architecture defines rules.
* Rules define classification.
* Classification drives sync behavior.

Knowledge Vault is the **source of truth**, not the filesystem.

